Claim type: bounded_theorem

For a fixed supplied finite plant and quantitative polynomial Lie certificate, the checked source composition replaces the designed positive one-port waveform by a static finite controller and compares every retained output throughout the compiler's actual finite observation window. Its sufficient inverse-accuracy resource powers include the growing compiler duration and waveform slew. A separate extension starts from a supplied correlated controller state and pays for a preparation-to-runtime switch. These are conditional finite-Hamiltonian implications.

The source decision `c93bcd9a29d2226e5923b5ac53bd1d1eead89e59abfe41e470557b4fbfae93c4`, recorded on 2026-10-15, accepts the root runtime construction with mandatory scope qualifications after reading the separately frozen extended derivation and source-exposed comparison. It also records rechecking of the extended release, phase and total allocation. It is neither an independent retained audit nor acceptance of this publication wrapper. The three original bodies below remain byte-for-byte unchanged, including their historical pending-status sentences. Their current interpretation is governed by this qualification and the preserved decision.

**The root runtime budget and the extended preparation-to-runtime budget are different complete contracts.** The root's phrase about a possible later release supplies no post-runtime stopping or decoupling theorem. The proved optional switch begins at the supplied preparation bit string. No permanent halt, restored controller, final isolation or reuse is concluded.

Primary-runner role: source integrity only. The proposed runner checks exact source bytes, interval recovery, declared inputs and later root binding evidence. It computes no Hamiltonian example, waveform, compiler search, resource experiment or proof test. The historical source proposal remains unexecuted. This canonical derivative requires separately captured frozen-draft and final-canonical root reviews before source-integrity execution; future execution or publication is not inferred. This source-only package records actual metadata assembly and inspection separately; integrity checks do not establish the mathematics.

