The [polynomial path mediator](POLYNOMIAL_PATH_MEDIATOR_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-10-15.md), 115,781 bytes, SHA256 `d0c250c80d25065d7b2667f22d83d53ef43419088fa7484f1c157a6408ac177f`, supplies two physically distinct Hamiltonian families. Its root proof occupies `[30425,48979)`, independent proof `[49121,84178)`, and exposed comparison `[84326,115781)`. The correlated-input preparation and preparation-to-runtime release premise is specifically the independent proof's section 10, canonical bytes `[75079,79497)`. Its exact-marginal lemma and earlier release comparison are traced through the mediator's basis-state-clock parent, canonical bytes `[94599,101646)` of SHA256 `0c3f1b569d41b75fa1c23e815e55f8481af640a9b292469e056541f698702ed1`. This is transitive premise provenance, not a separately invented preparation theorem. The exact parent/body/section identities and source-decision records are in the packet; Git ancestry alone adds no mathematical premise.

