## Runtime construction and sufficient resources

Put `R=ell(2nu+1)`, `P=R+2d(R+1)`. Invoke the specified compiler at nominal trace tolerance `epsilon/4`. With fixed-data constants absorbing that substitution, it returns `T<=C_T epsilon^-P` and a positive C1 waveform with Lipschitz bound `L_C<=C_L epsilon^-(R+1)`. Its scalar coefficient is at most `g`, while its full norm is at most `2g`. Zero endpoint derivatives make its zero extension through `[T,T+w]` C1 without an extra pulse-count factor in the Lipschitz bound.

Set `tau=T+w`, `H_P=H+R_s I+lambda J`, with a uniform bound `h_*>=||H_P||` and `R_s>=||H||`. The protected positive-splitting recipe has `T=2t0 sum_negative q_i>=2t0`; hence `Omega=pi/(2tau)<=pi/(4t0)`. A separately verified empty schedule has its own static/zero-time case. It is not inserted into `Omega` when `T=w=0`.

Choose the minimal ceiling `n=max(1,ceil[L_C^2 tau^4/(2 eta_X^2)])`, `m=n+4`. The controller adds `2m-3` sites and `3m-7` declared geometric edges, with maximum new-site degree three and one old/new port adjacency. Vanishing source coefficients do not remove the distinction between declared geometric edges and nonzero interactions. Define the common size exponent

```
M=4P+2R+4.
```

For the two complete physical families, preserve all actual inverse entries, complex source coefficients, the nonscalar `kappa n_p` counterterm, clock counterterms and positive source-block reserves:

| Quantity | Root mediator family | Independent mediator family |
|---|---|---|
| Unscaled mass and port parameter | `mu=m^-3`, `q=1/m` | `mu=m^-2`, `q=sqrt(G)`, `G=max(1,g)` |
| Complete nonvacuum inverse norm | `m^3` | `m^2` |
| Selected penalty | `Delta=M_R m^12/eta_med^2` | `Delta=M_I m^8/eta_med^2` |
| Penalty inverse-accuracy exponent | `2P+12M+2` | `2P+8M+2` |
