exp[-i Phi(t)] |vac_A> tensor chi_tau(t)
    tensor exp(-isH) W exp[-i(T+sigma)H],
Phi(t)=R_pos[t+integral_0^sigma u(v)dv]
       +(R_s+lambda j0)(t+sigma)+A_s+theta.
```

Without that correction the actual `exp(-i sigma H_P)` factor must remain. The `h0` scalar inside literal `H` already belongs to its background factors. A cubic monotone release has `integral u=sigma/2`, slew allowance `(3/(2sigma))(B_F+k nu_p)` and ideal regular closed-system work allowance `B_F+k nu_p`; endpoint/variation faults need their own contract. Only under the stated logarithmic preparation-gap recipe do the source's sufficient inverse-duration and slew powers `B_f+1` and `2B_f+1` apply. An independently larger preparation norm stays explicit.

