All source-sample, scalar, installed-coefficient, omitted-edge, old-background, release and runtime faults share the chosen integrated full-space allowance. Ideal one-head contractions do not authorize one-head-only fault bounds. At most `10m` new physical Pauli coefficient slots give the root's sufficient runtime tolerance `epsilon/(160 tau m)` only when they use the entire runtime defect allowance and other errors use none. The extended allowance includes release duration and fixed old slots. Positive parametrizations or paid peak reserves are separate from an integral error bound; whole positivity of `H_P` does not supply a positive decomposition of every literal old channel.

With ideal bare input and zero initial sample, both families retain

