The covariance is retained. These are moments of the full static generator on its ideal input. For trace error `e` and a fixed specified observable of full norm `B`, safe mean/second-moment/variance discrepancies are `Be`, `B^2e`, `3B^2e`. The growing controller norm therefore prevents the trace allocation alone from supplying vanishing energy-moment discrepancies. Static total-moment conservation and zero explicit runtime drive work do not identify physical energy, prepared energy cost or actuator work. Accurate moments of the evolving product comparator require a separate argument.

The supplied conditions still include certificate procurement, computable nominal matrices and sample evaluation, physical path/controller installation, whole-lifetime isolation, controller-state delivery, preparation-stage isolation, switching and timing/calibration. The actual delivered old marginal is retained; an earlier nominal source state needs a separate delivery-time/evolution contract. Native preparation, finite cooling, detector/energy identification, practical efficiency, common hardware caps, permanent stopping, final isolation and reuse remain unproved here. These are limits of the conditional result, not universal impossibility claims. The appendices preserve the concrete failed substitutions without expanding them into new no-go results.

