# Conditional autonomous realization of the accuracy-scaled one-port compiler

Status: new provisional analytic composition, not independently checked or root-accepted. This note combines accepted conditional sources at their exact stated interfaces and rederives the resource substitution. It is source-exposed, from the same model/effort and the author of several earlier proofs and comparisons. No root exponent calculation, other worker construction, scientific program, numerical compiler instance or physical device was consulted. The result remains conditional on actual finite Hamiltonians, supplied computable certificates, physical initialization/isolation and a supplied finite release. It is not a native controller or a retained theorem.

The composition is possible at the stated same-time complete-output interface. The external compiler's growing duration and slew must enter the autonomous clock and mediator sizes. A fixed-input mediator exponent cannot be copied unchanged. A finite output window retains a moving known clock state, not a stopped endpoint clock. Actual release ages the plant under a baseline containing the added path; the resulting extra path evolution must be retained or charged before asserting aging under the original H.

## 1. Exact imported results and supplied data

Use accuracy-scaled candidate 6cae05fe, its separate k0 readout 899a28b9, assessment c9c09872 and current root source acceptance e0735ca8. Their direct compiler is dd6cca85, with exposed comparison 227180a0 and qualified root acceptance 9f90d834. Use either of the two complete polynomial mediator families: root 45c211e6 or protected 0620431a, keeping their different physical parameters; their comparison is 3cc7a9d3 and root decision 8f26be5f. The task's fbc6c8f4 names the assembled publication note; its fully read 29,774-byte wrapper.md is c20ab3da, as resolved against BUILD_RESULT.json and the draft freeze. That wrapper is interpretation/provenance, not an additional mathematical independence claim. Exact full identities and recoverable sources are in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json.

The finite old plant P includes every old factor, memory, dirty filler and record. Its dimension d>=2 is fixed, and all plant inputs may be correlated with an arbitrary retained passive reference. It occupies the accepted nonnegative lattice box with an accessible corner port. The supplied complete ordinary-NN two-qubit/onsite H is unchanged, including H0. The added positive path J and one-port X/Y interface are the accepted ones. Fix norm bounds h>=||H||, j>=||J||, b>=||Jbar||, a scalar reserve R_s>=h, a time unit t0>0, port bound g>0, finite observation window w>=0, and complete computable target W with phase lift theta. All physical units stay fixed.

Fix the actual augmented polynomial/tree certificate, all its coefficient bounds, degree D, tree leaf maximum ell, and either nu=D (original recipe) or nu=k0 (separately accepted sharpening). These data do not depend on the requested accuracy. Polynomial-coordinate consistency and computability, certificate discovery and arbitrary oracle runtime remain supplied obligations. Set

    R = ell(2nu+1),
    P = R+2d(R+1).

The exact external sufficient recipe at tolerance epsilon_c has, for fixed admitted data,

    T <= C_T epsilon_c^(-P),
    N <= C_N epsilon_c^(-R),
    1/(t0 rho) <= C_rho epsilon_c^(-(R+1)),
    lambda in [epsilon_c/(2L_win), epsilon_c/L_win).

The constants C_T,C_N,C_rho are explicitly given in c9c09872 section 5. They include the full augmented dimension 2d and actual recurrence times. This note uses the specified sufficient ceilings, not arbitrarily larger repetitions or penalties.

For definiteness let the final full unhalved trace tolerance be 0<epsilon<=1 and choose epsilon_c=epsilon/4. Without an implemented external waveform defect, the accepted compiler's nominal complete trace error is at most epsilon_c on its window. No external actuator is actually run in this composition: that nominal waveform is data used to construct a static controller. Errors in its implemented static realization are charged below, not counted as a nonexistent external experiment.

## 2. The actual autonomous input waveform and horizon

For each accuracy first compute the accepted positive C1 port waveform C_e(t) on [0,T]. On active segments it is

    C_e(t)=g f(t)(I+sigma P_p),  P_p in {X_p,Y_p},

with zero value and derivative at every segment endpoint. Extend it by zero throughout [T,T+w]. Put

    tau=T+w,
    H_P=H+R_s I+lambda J,
    h_P<=h+R_s+j=:h_*.

Then H_P>=0 and remains ordinary-NN/onsite, and

    C_e(t)=a(t)I+b_x(t)X_p+b_y(t)Y_p,
    sqrt(b_x(t)^2+b_y(t)^2)<=a(t)<=g,
    C_e(0)=C_e(tau)=0,
    L_e=3g/(t0rho)

is a sufficient operator Lipschitz bound. The full pulse norm is at most 2g; g in the mediator hypothesis bounds its scalar coefficient, not its full norm. Concatenation does not introduce an extra factor N into the Lipschitz bound because derivatives vanish at joins and their global supremum is bounded. The extension through the idle window is C1.

Computable durations, cubic pieces, certified boundaries and the global modulus make the waveform sample values computable, including a sample at a segment boundary. No exact equality test of an irrational sample with a boundary is needed for certified approximate evaluation. All cost of that evaluation remains distinct from the finite resource bounds.

The explicit dd6cca85 recipe is nonempty even for a simple target: its positive coefficient splitting uses nonempty commutator words. Signed balance gives T=2t0 sum_negative q_i, hence T>=2t0. Thus tau has a fixed positive lower bound and

    tau<=C_tau epsilon^(-P),
    L_e<=C_L epsilon^(-(R+1)),
    Omega=pi/(2tau)<=pi/(4t0),

where one may take C_tau=4^P C_T+w and C_L=3g 4^(R+1) C_rho. This lower horizon bound is needed to control the clock's 1/tau factors. It is not a prescribed completion time.

Zero-runtime branches are kept separate. If a separately verified compiler branch returns an empty waveform, that branch is already static and needs no waveform controller. Its asserted target/error still has to be verified. In particular, T=w=0 must not be inserted into Omega=pi/(2tau); use the zero-time identity map with its already declared target error and no new controller. If an empty waveform has w>0, the static H_P evolution itself handles that interval. This bypass makes no nontrivial gate or reset follow from zero elapsed time. The resource family below concerns the nonempty dd6cca85 recipe.

## 3. Clock size, both mediator recipes and exact finite constants

Choose isometry budgets eta_X=eta_med=epsilon/16. The minimal sufficient clock choice is

    n=max(1,ceil[L_e^2 tau^4/(2eta_X^2)]),
    r=n+1, m=n+4, Omega=pi/(2tau).

The same accepted exterior geometry adds 2m-3 sites and 3m-7 declared geometric edges; it preserves the old plant and all its factors. Its maximum new-site degree is three. Source coefficients may vanish. Every unlisted physical edge or field over the whole lifetime is either actually isolated or included in a complete-space fault bound.

The positive-edge clock has exact full norm B_X=Omega n(n+1), scalar B_X/2 and known full vector

    chi_tau(t)=exp(-iOmega n t) sum_j sqrt(binomial(n,j))
         cos(Omega t)^(n-j)[i sin(Omega t)]^j |j>.

Its initial state is one at c_0 and zero on the other clock bits. Store C_j=C_e(Omega^-1 arcsin sqrt(j/n)). The uniform clock isometry error is at most L_e tau^2/sqrt(2n)<=eta_X. In particular the free comparison vector has chi_tau(tau)=|n> including phase. Its binomial distribution is not assumed to be the actual interacting clock distribution.

For either family write

    L_A=sum_path(n_v+n_w-S_vw)+mu N_A,
    t_j=(L_path+mu I)^(-1)_(a,u_j),
    gamma_v=(L_path+mu I)^(-1)_(v,v),
    z_j=-(b_x,j+i b_y,j)/(2q t_j),
    V=q(XX+YY)_(p,a)+sum_j n_j[Re(z_j)X_(u_j)+Im(z_j)Y_(u_j)],
    v=2q+sum_j|z_j|,
    kappa=4q^2 gamma_a, d_j=|z_j|^2 gamma_(u_j),
    C_ct=kappa n_p+sum_j d_j n_j.

Keep these physically different choices separate:

| Data | Root family R | Independent family I |
|---|---|---|
| mu, q | m^-3, 1/m | m^-2, sqrt(G), G=max(1,g) |
| Full nonvacuum inverse | m^3 | m^2 |
| Response certificate | all entries >=7m^2/8 | endpoint entries >=m/2 |
| Full counterterm allowance c_f | 9/2+(18r/49)g^2 | 8mG+2G |
| v allowance | V_R=2+g | 3sqrt(G) |
| ell_A=||L_A|| | 2(m-1)+m^-2 | 2(m-1)+m^-1 |

Both auxiliary vacua are unique, with full-sector lower bound L_A>=mu N_A. The inverse includes the two-excitation sector. The nonscalar port counterterm remains. On the one-clock-head input sector, the exact contraction is J_A* V R_A V J_A=C_ct-sum_j n_j(b_x,j X_p+b_y,j Y_p). It is not a multihead identity and uses arbitrary complete plant inputs.

Set A=H_P+K_X+sum a_j n_j+C_ct. Install the static

    K=H_P+F=Delta L_A+sqrt(Delta)V+A+R_pos I,
    R_pos=sqrt(Delta)v.

All new blocks are positive after distributing the source reserve as 2q sqrt(Delta)I on the port edge and sqrt(Delta)|z_j|I on source edge j. Thus F>=0. Old H_P whole positivity suffices for this operator theorem; any requirement that every old channel be separately positive still needs an explicit supplied decomposition/reserves. Semidefinite blocks need positive parametrization or paid local fault margins under actual calibration errors.

Use the following exact accepted sufficient majorants, evaluated at the actual tau and h_*; their tau dependence is not frozen away. For R put

    C_R=9/2+(18/49)g^2,
    D_R0=2h_*+2Omega+3g+C_R,
    A_R1=2V_R+tau D_R0 V_R+tau V_R^3,
    A_R2=2V_R^2+tau D_R0 V_R^2,
    M_R=1+4A_R1^2+2A_R2,
    Delta_R=M_R m^12/eta_med^2.

For I put

    D_I0=2h_*+2Omega+13G,
    C_I1=6sqrt(G)+3tau D_I0 sqrt(G)+27tau G^(3/2),
    C_I2=18G+9tau D_I0 G,
    M_I=1+4C_I1^2+2C_I2,
    Delta_I=M_I m^8/eta_med^2.

The R majorant is attributed to exposed comparison 3cc7a9d3; the I majorant belongs to 0620431a. The bare-input corrector, including both bare-versus-dressed endpoint terms, bounds the mediator isometry error by eta_med. No prepared dressed state is required. The complete full norm allowance is

    B=a_*+Delta ell_A+2sqrt(Delta)v,
    a_*=h_*+B_X+rg+c_f.

Every formula here is finite and computable from supplied nominal samples and the earlier compiler output. It establishes a resource recipe, not a bound on arbitrary-real oracle time.

## 4. Derivation of the composite powers

Define the clock-size exponent

    A_cl=4P+2R+4.

Indeed L_e^2 tau^4/eta_X^2 has sufficient exponent 2(R+1)+4P+2=A_cl. The minimal ceiling gives, for example,

    m<=C_m epsilon^(-A_cl),
    C_m=6+128 C_L^2 C_tau^4.

For either family tau Omega=pi/2, all other h_*,g constants are fixed, and tau>=2t0. Inspection of the displayed M_f therefore gives a computable constant Mbar_f with

    M_f<=Mbar_f(1+tau)^2<=Mtilde_f epsilon^(-2P).

One need not use asymptotics to select Delta: use the exact formulas in section 3. This observation only derives their uniform powers. It shows explicitly the factor epsilon^-2P that would be lost by importing the mediator's fixed-tau accuracy powers unchanged.

Let B_Rexp=2P+13A_cl+2 and B_Iexp=2P+9A_cl+2. The resulting sufficient exponents are:

| Quantity, as an O(epsilon^-exponent) upper recipe | R exponent | I exponent |
|---|---:|---:|
| Clock/auxiliary size, site and edge counts | A_cl | A_cl |
| Unscaled reduced-inverse norm | 3A_cl | 2A_cl |
| Delta; largest auxiliary edge block | 2P+12A_cl+2 | 2P+8A_cl+2 |
| Full norm and absolute scalar allowance | B_Rexp | B_Iexp |
| Runtime norm action tau B | 3P+13A_cl+2 | 3P+9A_cl+2 |
| R_pos | P+6A_cl+1 | P+4A_cl+1 |
| Physical port XX/YY coefficient | P+5A_cl+1 | P+4A_cl+1 |
| Physical source coefficient allowance | P+5A_cl+1 | P+3A_cl+1 |
| Scaled auxiliary mass Delta mu | 2P+9A_cl+2 | 2P+6A_cl+2 |
| Ideal bare-input mean | P+6A_cl+1 | P+4A_cl+1 |
| Ideal bare-input variance | 2P+10A_cl+2 | 2P+8A_cl+2 |

The powers follow from the explicit monomials, not by dividing independent big-O statements. For example Delta_R/m^2=M_R m^10/eta_med^2 gives the root variance term; Delta_I G=M_I G m^8/eta_med^2 gives the independent term. Likewise source and port powers use the exact q and response bounds of the chosen family. All coefficients, clock norm, counterterm sums and source reserves are included in B. The two constructions may not be mixed to obtain a third unproved Hamiltonian.

These are very loose sufficient powers in inverse accuracy at fixed admitted certificate and finite plant dimension. They do not claim optimality, polynomial scaling in qubit count, polynomial-time coefficient oracles, bounded hardware strengths or practical construction. The new clock dimension and m depend on the already enormous compiler duration. The selected scaled auxiliary gap is not a gap theorem for the full interacting K.

## 5. Complete same-time target before release

Let J_bare append the clock endpoint string and auxiliary vacuum to the complete old input. Uniformly for 0<=t<=tau,

    ||exp(-itK)J_bare
       -exp(-itR_pos)|vac_A> tensor chi_tau(t) tensor U_C(t)||
       <=eta_X+eta_med.

Here U_C is generated by the actual nominal H_P+C_e. For t=T+s, 0<=s<=w, the external compiler gives its full old-plant target

    V_old(t)=exp(-i chi_e(t)) exp(-isH) W exp(-iTH),
    chi_e(t)=(R_s+lambda j0)t+A_s+theta,
    A_s=g sum_active(t_l-t0rho).

Consequently the joint autonomous target at the same runtime t is

    exp[-i(R_pos t+chi_e(t))]
       |vac_A> tensor chi_tau(t) tensor exp(-isH)W exp(-iTH).

It includes every auxiliary, clock, old/reference output and the prescribed coherent phase. The actual total controller state need not be the free clock vector; the estimate compares the complete actual isometry to that vector. Tensoring an arbitrary reference preserves the operator bound; passage to full unhalved trace distance costs exactly a factor at most two.

Only at t=tau=T+w is the comparison clock at |n>. At t=T, when w>0, its known state is generally a coherent intermediate clock vector. Thus the finite old-plant readiness window composes with a time-dependent complete controller target. It does not yield a stopped pure endpoint clock over the whole window, or a return to its initial state. A consumer demanding that stronger fixed controller output needs another construction. A prescribed earlier unaged old input is also not the target.

## 6. Supplied input, finite release and corrected actual-aging phase

The ideal starting controller is a known computational-basis product string; it remains a supplied state, not a cooling conclusion. An arbitrary actual delivered joint state sigma_CY may correlate the controller C with the entire old/reference system Y. Let omega_Y=Tr_C sigma be its exact unconditional marginal and delta its bad population relative to the required pure controller projector. The accepted pure-factor lemma gives

    ||sigma_CY-P_C tensor omega_Y||_1
      <=g_pure(delta):=delta+sqrt(delta(4-3delta))<=3sqrt(delta).

This replacement uses no conditioning, successful outcome or nominal pre-delivery old state. A supplied Gibbs controller marginal for k=2m-3 preparation bits, gap nu_p and inverse temperature beta has delta_G<=k exp(-beta nu_p). A half-trace marginal delivery error d_p gives delta<=delta_G+d_p (capped at one). The marginal's 2delta_G distance is not a full joint replacement bound without actual product independence.

For example, g_pure(delta)<=epsilon/8 follows by requiring

    delta_G<=epsilon^2/1152, d_p<=epsilon^2/1152,
    beta nu_p>=log(1152k/epsilon^2).

At fixed supplied beta>0, choosing nu_p by that last formula gives preparation norm k nu_p=O(epsilon^-A_cl log(1/epsilon)). This is a supplied equilibrium/delivery contract. No finite cooling time, actuator or state supplier follows. All prior source waiting is incorporated in the actual delivered omega_Y, or needs its own earlier-time contract. Runtime interactions must be isolated or actually compensated while the preparation premise is asserted.

The optional finite release uses the accepted positive interpolation

    H_rel(v)=H_P+(1-u(v))G_prep+u(v)F,
    0<=v<=sigma, u(0)=0, u(sigma)=1,

where G_prep annihilates the ideal bit string and F=K-H_P>=0. This requires supplied switching; runtime after it is static. The plant ages during release under H_P, not just H. That distinction cannot be dropped.

The following explicitly phased estimate is a new derivation within this provisional composition. Define F0=F-R_pos I and a computable B_F>=||F|| from the positive-block norm sum. Then ||F0||<=B_F+R_pos=:B_rel. Comparing the exact release to

    exp(-iR_pos integral_0^sigma u(v)dv)
       |controller_0> tensor exp(-i sigma H_P)

has residual u(v)F0 on that comparison vector; the G_prep term vanishes there. Hence its isometry error is at most B_rel integral u<=B_rel sigma. This extraction keeps the installed scalar explicitly rather than removing it physically.

Further, full-space Duhamel gives

    ||exp(-i sigma H_P)
       -exp[-i(R_s+lambda j0)sigma]exp(-i sigma H)||
       <=lambda b sigma.

Choose eta_rel=epsilon/16 and, in the fixed reference units, a positive fixed rate b0 (one is allowed) and

    sigma=eta_rel/(B_rel+lambda b+b0).

Then the combined release-plus-extra-path-aging isometry error is <=eta_rel. All runtime estimates hold for the resulting H-aged old/reference input because their plant-input domain is arbitrary. At actual total time sigma+T+s, the complete comparator becomes

    exp(-i Phi(t)) |vac_A> tensor chi_tau(t)
       tensor exp(-isH)W exp[-i(T+sigma)H],  t=T+s,

    Phi(t)=R_pos[t+integral_0^sigma u(v)dv]
           +(R_s+lambda j0)(t+sigma)+A_s+theta.

This phase includes the runtime reserve, its extracted release area, the compiler static scalar through actual elapsed time, the smoothed positive pulse area and target phase lift. The scalar h0 inside literal H is already in its two background factors. The clock phase remains in chi_tau(t). G_prep and auxiliary penalty scalars cancel on their ideal eigenvectors only with their nonidentity terms; their full operator scalars and actual release generators are still paid. The residual release terms are charged, not assumed zero.

Without the extra lambda b sigma allowance, the legitimate target is instead U_C(t)exp(-i sigma H_P), with its own exact phase. Stating pure H aging while retaining neither that factor nor the correction would be a real composition error. This note explicitly chooses the charged correction, not a hidden ability to turn off lambda J during release.

For a cubic monotone release, max|u'|=3/(2sigma) and integral u=sigma/2. Its full slew and work allowances are

    slew <=(3/(2sigma))(B_F+k nu_p),
    |W_rel|<=||F-G_prep||<=B_F+k nu_p.

The work formula assumes regular closed dynamics; actual endpoint/variation defects need their own bound. The exact interpolated scalar is s_(H_P)+(1-u)s_(G_prep)+u s_F. Source installation, cooling and reset work are not inferred from this finite interpolation.

For either family's exponent B_fexp above, sigma^-1 has sufficient power B_fexp+1. With fixed beta and the logarithmic gap prescription, k nu_p grows more slowly than the sufficient polynomial B_F bound, giving a sufficient release-slew power 2B_fexp+1 and release-work allowance O(epsilon^-B_fexp). These describe a particular positive release recipe. Any independently larger preparation norm must remain explicitly in the formula and may change the price. Runtime norm action is tau B; preparation time/action is not bounded by the supplied Gibbs premise.

## 7. One combined error budget, physical precision and moments

One consistent complete unhalved trace allocation is

    epsilon_c=epsilon/4,
    g_pure(delta)<=epsilon/8,
    eta_X=eta_med=eta_rel=eta_cal=eta_time=epsilon/16.

Use eta_cal for the total integrated full-generator defect over release and runtime, and eta_time for any additional fixed-target timing displacement. Then the complete error is at most

    epsilon_c+epsilon/8
      +2(eta_X+eta_med+eta_rel+eta_cal+eta_time)=epsilon.

All simultaneous calibration, unlisted-edge, coefficient, source-sampling and scalar defects share eta_cal; none may independently spend that whole budget. Actual source delivery is already counted in delta, and actual plant aging is in the comparator. The release coefficient error and runtime coefficient error must be included over their actual durations. The comparison is not restricted to a one-clock-head fault sector.

For actual installed full generator K', a sufficient constant runtime norm-error rate is proportional to epsilon/(tau+sigma), with inverse allowance O(epsilon^-(P+1)). Large generator norm alone does not add an extra factor B to this absolute rate; it does make relative precision much more demanding. The supplied explicit layout has at most 10m new physical Pauli coefficient slots. Including finitely many fixed old slots, a conservative per-slot physical absolute tolerance is

    delta_phys<=eta_cal/[(10m+c_old)(tau+sigma)],

after allocating release errors consistently. Its inverse has sufficient power A_cl+P+1. For coefficients of size Delta, a relative tolerance using the displayed recipe has inverse power 3P+13A_cl+3 for R or 3P+9A_cl+3 for I. Equivalently unscaled mass/edge precision must pay the additional Delta in the full generator estimate. Positive weighted-path and mass certificates, or paid block reserves, remain separate from this coordinate norm budget. Recomputing a favorable response after a parameter error does not remove the actual generator discrepancy against the fixed target.

A fixed-target observation-time error can be charged by B_actual|delta_t| in isometry norm, giving a sufficient inverse timing tolerance of power B_fexp+1. If timing instead changes the intended actual-time target, its clock state, old aging and all scalar phases must be updated explicitly. Native timing or switching precision is not supplied by the polynomial bounds.

The exact full normalized runtime scalar is

    s_K=s_(H_P)+B_X/2+(sum_j a_j)/2
        +Delta[m-1+mu m/2]+kappa/2+(sum_j d_j)/2+R_pos.

It is distinct from the prepared mean. For ideal bare input and C_e(0)=0, set D_P=H_P+kappa n_p. The exact initial mean and variance are

    mean=Tr(rho_P D_P)+Omega n+R_pos,
    variance=Var_(rho_P)(D_P)+Omega^2 n
                           +4Delta q^2 Tr(rho_P n_p).

They include the H_P/n_p covariance and every reserve. The powers in section 4 follow. Under exact static runtime these total moments are conserved. Static runtime has no explicit drive-work term; that does not identify actuator energy or make release/installation/preparation free. The external compiler's small endpoint work estimate is not a bound on the autonomous controller's prepared energy.

For the same declared observable of norm B_O, complete state error e gives mean discrepancy <=B_O e, second-moment discrepancy <=B_O^2 e and variance discrepancy <=3B_O^2 e. Here B_O may grow like B. Thus epsilon-accurate output states do not give vanishing full-energy moment errors against the product comparator. In particular the upper allowances B epsilon and B^2 epsilon can grow. The separate mediator leakage allowance Delta ell_A eta_med^2 need not vanish either.

For accurate actual static total moments relative to the ideal bare preparation, source/release errors can be tightened after choosing K, paying e_init<=epsilon_m/(3B^2) as needed, with new release and preparation prices. That does not automatically establish accurate moments of the runtime product comparator, whose discrepancy also includes the simulation error. No stronger energy-accuracy, thermalization, detector or reuse result is claimed.

## 8. What closes, what remains open, and evidence

The following composition is justified provisionally by the displayed argument: a supplied fixed quantitative polynomial certificate gives a finite positive one-port waveform; a supplied basis-start controller with either separately priced mediator reproduces that waveform on the full plant/reference domain; a supplied sufficiently accurate controller state and finite positive release give the stated actual-time full-output window with complete scalar accounting. Finite geometry, unique auxiliary vacuum, full-sector inverse, nonscalar counterterms, bare endpoints and actual clock output are retained. The resource powers are explicit conditional upper recipes.

The result does not close physical realization from native states or axioms. It requires complete nominal matrices, sample access, polynomial certificate procurement, path installation, selected coefficients, isolation, controller-state delivery, source-stage isolation, fast release and sufficiently accurate timing/calibration. No finite cooling time follows. The full source-to-runtime chronology from an earlier nominal state remains open without a source delivery-time/evolution contract. Whole positivity is not local-block positivity of every old term. The observation window does not halt, isolate, restore or recycle the controller. Full-energy comparison accuracy remains a separate problem. No uniform hardware cap or efficient general compiler in qubit number is obtained.

Failure routes preserved include importing fixed-tau mediator powers while tau grows; using a one-head inverse for the two-excitation corrector; dropping kappa n_p; using multihead or vacuum clock input as a launch; omitting the two bare-input endpoints; replacing inverse-sine samples by linear position samples; losing the clock or reserve phase; taking arbitrary oversized n/Delta; replacing a correlated Gibbs marginal by a product state at cost 2delta; asserting original-H aging through release without charging lambda Jbar; treating the moving clock window as a fixed endpoint; and inferring energy accuracy from small trace error with growing B. These are scoped failures, not a universal no-go.

This note was derived after complete source exposure to the supplied prior results, but without any new root exponent calculation. The earlier protected statuses belong to their frozen sources and do not transfer to this composition. The complete root mediator argument, comparison, current wrapper and acceptances were read; earlier complete author/read coverage of the other exact bodies was reused, with the independent mediator's resource/calibration/release sections reread. An initial combined read truncated the comparison/wrapper presentation; both were reread in complete bounded outputs before use. No source was changed.

No scientific execution, compiler search, numerical fixture, external literature search or new agent occurred. The historical wrapper mentions one earlier root finite scientific fixture; it was not reopened or rerun and supplies no proof of this new composition. Metadata helpers record exact selected sources, recovery, coverage and actual subprocess receipts only. No W/C checkout, Git/PR, checkpoint, lock, prompt, physical axiom or audit status changed. This is one new provisional derivation awaiting separate checking, not a completed physical supplier theorem or a root acceptance.


